--TEST--
An enum case that does not exist, written as a field value of an anonymous object, is `E0309` once, as it is anywhere else: at a call argument, with the nearest case as its help, nested in a second object, through a class-scoped enum and through a component's enum. It never reaches code generation
--FILE--
<?nvs
enum Color { Red = 1 }

class Shop {
    enum Size { Small = 1 }

    public static function paint({ color: Color } $options): int {
        return 1;
    }

    public static function pack({ box: { size: Shop::Size } } $options): int {
        return 2;
    }
}

echo Shop::paint({ color: Color::Blue }), "\n";
echo Shop::paint({ color: Color::Rd }), "\n";
echo Shop::pack({ box: { size: Shop::Size::Large } }), "\n";
echo Novis\Intl\DateFormat::dates([Core\Time\Date::at(2026, 1, 5)], 'en',
    { length: Novis\Intl\DateFormat::Length::Huge })[0], "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0309]: `Color` has no constant named `Blue`
   --> case.nvs:16:27
%A
error[E0309]: `Color` has no constant named `Rd`
   --> case.nvs:17:27
%A
   = help: did you mean `Red`?
%A
error[E0309]: `Shop::Size` has no constant named `Large`
   --> case.nvs:18:32
%A
error[E0309]: `Novis\Intl\DateFormat::Length` has no constant named `Huge`
   --> case.nvs:20:15
%A
error: aborting due to 4 errors
